 ### Fixed
 
+- `OrchestratorHooks.onError` now fires on every rejection inside a turn, not only when the thrown value is `instanceof Error`. Previously, a rejection with a string, plain object, or `undefined` bypassed `onError` completely while still rejecting to the caller. Non-`Error` values are wrapped in an `Error` with a readable `message` and the original value preserved on `error.cause`; an `Error` instance still reaches `onError` as the same instance, and the value re-thrown to the caller is unchanged. **Migration note**: an `onError` hook will now be called on non-`Error` rejections it previously missed, and can read `error.cause` when it needs the raw rejection value.
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).
 
 ## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-29
